>  I think you're on to something there.  Conducts can make 
>Nethack nearly impossible.  If that's not enough, then players 
>aren't really interested in a more difficult Nethack.

Eh, I'm not that intersted in "that kind of challenge."  Its like
saying, 'well, this racing game is too easy, so I'll try to make it
harder by giving the comp a head start.'  Sure it makes it harder, but
not in a very fun way. 

 In a sense you are holding back to fight against a weaker opponent,
rather than giving your all to try to overcome an insurmountable
opponent.  Both can be challenges, but giving your best to try to win
instead of holding back makes it far more fun.

