I don't know about you, but Gehennom was terribly boring for me even
when it was my first time going into it.  The Valley of the dead was
cool and 'scary' but once I got into the mazes?  Boring.  I was only
mostly spoiled on above castle stuff at this point (I didn't even know
about vlad's tower, etc, and had to ask around when I got to the
bottom and no idea what to do) and even then it was dull.  The main
thing keeping me going was in hopes that there would be a 3rd section
of the dungeon much more interesting like the first.

The reason I still slog through all that, is because I like the very
end of the game.  The planes, being chased by the wizard, sacrificing
the amulet, etc.  Its an extremely intense moment that I've been
building up to.  Its a shame I have to slog through Gehennom to get
there.


